Subject: install a HIP backend that is not built against ROCm

The HIP install path bundles ROCm's own payload next to the backend module: its BLAS libraries,
its code-object manager and its Tensile kernel files, and it stops the configure when the
code-object manager is absent. A HIP build does not have to stand on a ROCm installation. This
one stands on our own HIP runtime for gfx1013, which brings its own two libraries and has no
code-object manager and no Tensile files at all.

The condition is the one the top of the same file already uses to select ROCm's compiler flags: a
runner directory named rocm_v* is a ROCm build, anything else is not. Every upstream build is
unchanged.
